 "notes": "All six old kinds kept; Bande dessinée album, Manga anthology magazine and Dōjinshi added. Collected-edition lines became archetypes (Masterworks, DC Archive, Deluxe, Epic Collection moved from Omnibus to softcover since it is a paperback line, Marvel/DC Omnibus, Image compendium, Absolute, Artist's Edition with Studio/Gallery/Art Edition equivalents, kanzenban, aizōban, sōshūhen, bunkoban); manga labels Jump Comics, Shōnen Magazine/Sunday/Champion Comics as archetypes. Kadokawa SKU labels trimmed to Kadokawa Comics Ace (Asuka, Beam, Bushiroad, Dengeki, Dragon Comics Age, Harta dropped); Marvel GN dropped as generic. Old 'Tankōbon', 'Wide-ban' models became t; Mighty Marvel Masterworks became a Masterworks version. Grading and variants went to t/dt plus a CGC archetype. No comic titles named. BD publishers are brand entries only (from knowledge) since no per-publisher album line was fetched."
